INSERT INTO `tec_oficios` (`id`, `oficio`, `descripcion`, `dtcreate`) VALUES
	(1, 'Mopping of Residential floors', 'The floors were first swept to remove loose dirt and debris. A cleaning solution was then applied using a mop, ensuring thorough coverage of all areas. The mop was regularly rinsed to maintain cleanliness. After mopping, the floors were allowed to air dry, leaving them spotless and hygienic.', '2024-06-18 17:19:41.000000'),
	(5, 'pool deck cleaning', 'Pool deck cleaning involves thoroughly cleaning the area surrounding the swimming pool to ensure it is safe and aesthetically pleasing. This task includes removing debris, such as leaves and dirt, and scrubbing the surface to eliminate algae and mildew. High-pressure washing may be used to remove stubborn stains and grime. Additionally, it’s important to clean and inspect the pool deck for any damage, such as cracks or loose tiles, to maintain structural integrity. Regular cleaning helps prevent slips and falls, ensuring a safe environment for pool users. Finally, the deck is rinsed and left to dry completely.', '2024-06-19 18:58:20.000000'),
	(6, 'Cleaning of Bathrooms', 'The bathroom cleaning process in a clubhouse involves several key steps to ensure cleanliness and hygiene. First, all trash is collected and disposed of properly. Next, toilets and urinals are scrubbed and disinfected thoroughly. Sinks, faucets, and countertops are then cleaned and polished. Mirrors are wiped down to remove smudges and streaks. Finally, floors are swept and mopped, and all supplies like soap, paper towels, and toilet paper are restocked.', '2024-06-25 02:01:46.000000'),
	(7, 'Window cleaning process in a clubhouse', 'The window cleaning process in a clubhouse involves several essential steps to ensure spotless and clear windows. First, any loose dirt or dust is removed using a dry cloth or brush. Then, a cleaning solution is applied to the glass surfaces. The windows are scrubbed with a sponge or microfiber cloth to remove grime and fingerprints. Next, a squeegee is used to wipe away the cleaning solution, leaving the glass streak-free. Finally, the window frames and sills are cleaned and dried to complete the process.', '2024-06-25 02:03:09.000000'),
	(8, 'Spider webb removal', 'The spider web removal process involves several precise steps to ensure all webs are eliminated. First, inspect the area to identify all spider webs. Next, use a long-handled duster or vacuum with an extension hose to remove the webs from ceilings, corners, and other hard-to-reach places. After removing the webs, wipe down surfaces with a damp cloth to catch any remaining web fragments. Finally, dispose of the collected webs and clean the equipment used.', '2024-06-25 02:04:30.000000'),
	(9, 'Removal of weeds', 'The weed removal process involves several key steps to ensure thorough eradication. First, inspect the area to identify all weed-infested spots. Next, use a hand tool or hoe to loosen the soil around the weeds, making it easier to pull them out by the roots. Carefully remove the weeds, ensuring the entire root is extracted to prevent regrowth. Dispose of the weeds properly, preferably in a compost bin. Finally, check the area again and apply mulch or a weed barrier to prevent future weed growth.', '2024-06-25 02:05:22.000000'),
	(10, 'Alignments of table and chairs', 'The alignment of tables and chairs involves several important steps to ensure a neat and organized setup. First, clear the area of any debris or obstacles. Next, place the tables in their designated positions according to the floor plan or layout. Ensure each table is level and stable. Then, arrange the chairs around each table, ensuring they are evenly spaced and aligned. Finally, step back to inspect the overall arrangement, making any necessary adjustments to maintain symmetry and order.', '2024-06-25 02:07:52.000000'),
	(11, 'Blower cleaning', 'The blower cleaning process involves several steps to ensure a thorough job. First, inspect the area to identify debris and dust. Next, use a leaf blower to direct air at high speed, clearing leaves, dirt, and other debris from sidewalks, patios, and other surfaces. Move systematically to ensure all areas are covered. After blowing, check for any remaining debris and remove it manually if necessary. Finally, turn off and clean the blower, ensuring it\'s ready for the next use.', '2024-06-25 14:13:37.000000'),
	(12, 'Mopping of floors', 'The mopping of floors involves several essential steps to ensure cleanliness. First, sweep or vacuum the floor to remove any loose dirt and debris. Next, prepare a bucket with warm water and a suitable floor cleaner. Dip the mop into the solution, wring out excess water, and mop the floor in a systematic pattern, such as back and forth or in a figure-eight motion. After mopping, allow the floor to air dry, or use a dry mop to speed up the process. Finally, rinse and clean the mop and bucket thoroughly.', '2024-06-25 14:14:27.000000'),
	(13, 'Elevator cleaning', 'The elevator cleaning process involves several crucial steps for thorough sanitation. First, the elevator is inspected for any trash or debris, which is then removed. Next, all surfaces, including buttons, handrails, and walls, are wiped down with a disinfectant cleaner. The floor is then swept and mopped, ensuring all corners are clean. Mirrors and metal surfaces are polished to remove smudges and fingerprints. Finally, the cleaning supplies are removed, and the elevator is checked to ensure it is spotless and ready for use.', '2024-06-25 14:21:28.000000'),
	(14, 'Spiderweb removal of resident hallway  ', 'The spider web removal process from floors involves several key steps to ensure thorough cleaning. First, inspect the floor area to locate all spider webs. Next, use a broom or vacuum with an extension hose to gently remove the webs from the floor surface and corners. After the webs are removed, sweep or vacuum the entire floor to catch any remaining debris. Then, mop the floor with a suitable cleaner to ensure it is spotless. Finally, dispose of the collected webs and clean the equipment used.', '2024-06-25 14:22:25.000000'),
	(15, 'Spiderweb removal of stairwell', 'The spider web removal process from a stairway involves several key steps to ensure thorough cleaning. First, inspect the stairway to identify all spider webs. Next, use a long-handled duster or vacuum with an extension hose to remove the webs from corners, railings, and steps. After removing the webs, wipe down surfaces with a damp cloth to catch any remaining fragments. Then, sweep or vacuum the stairs to remove any additional debris. Finally, dispose of the collected webs and clean the equipment used.', '2024-06-25 14:22:57.000000'),
	(16, 'Cleaning of handle rails', 'The cleaning of handrails involves several important steps to ensure they are hygienic and spotless. First, remove any loose dirt and debris with a dry cloth or duster. Next, apply a suitable cleaner or disinfectant to the handrails. Wipe down the entire surface with a microfiber cloth, paying special attention to areas frequently touched. After cleaning, dry the handrails with a clean, dry cloth to prevent water spots or streaks. Finally, inspect the handrails to ensure they are thoroughly cleaned and polished.', '2024-06-25 14:23:40.000000'),
	(17, 'Cleaning of mailbox', 'The cleaning of mailboxes involves several steps to ensure they are clean and well-maintained. First, remove any mail and debris from the mailbox. Next, use a soft brush or cloth to dust off loose dirt and cobwebs. Apply a suitable cleaner to the inside and outside surfaces, then wipe down thoroughly with a microfiber cloth. Pay special attention to the handle and keyhole, ensuring they are sanitized. Finally, dry the mailbox with a clean cloth to prevent water spots and rust.', '2024-06-25 14:24:29.000000'),
	(18, 'Cleaning of trash rooms', 'The cleaning of trash rooms involves several essential steps to ensure hygiene and odor control. First, remove all trash bags and debris from the room. Next, sweep and mop the floor using a strong disinfectant cleaner. Wipe down walls, doors, and trash bins with a sanitizing solution to eliminate any stains and bacteria. Clean and disinfect high-touch areas like door handles and light switches. Finally, ensure proper ventilation to reduce odors and leave the room smelling fresh.', '2024-06-25 14:25:12.000000');
